#!/bin/sh
# Run the whole gate before a push.
#
# This is a courtesy that shortens the loop and it is not the enforcement. It
# lives in a clone's local git configuration, it is absent from a fresh clone
# until somebody points core.hooksPath at this directory, and anybody who reads
# this file can see the one flag that skips it. What stands behind a merge is the
# ruleset on the default branch and the checks that run on the pull request.
#
# One line, and it states nothing of its own. Everything the gate does, the order
# it does it in and what it says about the legs it did not run are in
# src/bin/gate.rs, so this file cannot drift away from the procedure. A test in
# that file reads this one and refuses any other command here.
#
# Skipping it is git push --no-verify, and it is written here rather than left to
# be discovered, because a hook whose escape hatch is a secret is a hook people
# work around by deleting.
exec cargo run --locked --quiet --bin gate
